      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 The Authors. Published by Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA.",
        "AbstractText": "A photolabile ruthenium-based complex, [Ru(bpy)2 (4AMP)2 ](PF6 )2 , (4AMP=4-(aminomethyl)pyridine) is incorporated into polyurea organo- and hydrogels via the reactive amine moieties on the photocleavable 4AMP ligands. While showing long-term stability in the dark, cleavage of the pyridine-ruthenium bond upon irradiation with visible or near-infrared irradiation (in a two-photon process) leads to rapid de-gelation of the supramolecular gels, thus enabling spatiotemporal micropatterning by photomasking or pulsed NIR-laser irradiation."
      },
